	(text "into FF1.D:  0/3.3 V CMOS at 10 MHz, edges ~1-2 ns"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 288.2900 151.1300 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5000 1.5000)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0df6a615-dca9-ba26-4b0a-28a8960686c5")
	)
	(text "out of FF2:  BEAT_12, ~1234 Hz square, 0/3.3 V  -  its EDGE TIME is the measurement"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 288.2900 156.2100 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5000 1.5000)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "654f0d9c-989e-5aa0-fde8-fecf4b4d8b99")
	)
	(text "HCLK_12:  10.0012 MHz, 0/3.3 V, this channel's own length-matched branch off the fan-out"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 288.2900 161.2900 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5000 1.5000)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a642cc0a-db4a-ae2b-3e46-f62d7a4e1105")
	)
	(text_box "THE 50R TERM, THE JUMPER SHIPS REMOVED.\nFit only if the source drives 50 ohm.  A ZED-F9T is DESTROYED\nby fitting it: its TIMEPULSE pin is 5 mA absolute maximum and\n3.3 V into 50R asks for 66 mA.\nConversely, leaving it out on an 8 Vpp open-circuit source\nfloats the gate input to about +7.4 V, over the 74LVC1GU04's\n6.5 V absolute maximum.  On this channel it should be FITTED."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.2400 148.5900 0)
		(size 95.2500 21.5900)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 220 220 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5e7957ca-4633-cf5f-3432-3864240d64eb")
	)
	(text_box "THE BAV99 CLAMP IS DNP.\nFit only on a channel you will run UNTERMINATED with a source above about 6 Vpp\nopen circuit.  It is not fitted by default because its reverse leakage flows in\nthe 1M self-bias resistor: 10 nA is 10 mV of bias shift, leakage roughly doubles\nevery 10 degC, and at ~825 mV/ns that would swamp the whole long-tau drift\nbudget."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.2400 204.4700 0)
		(size 121.9200 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 245 210 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66c32cc3-1a5a-b15f-3599-7bc67e6c12e0")
	)
	(text_box "THE SAMPLING FLIP-FLOP (FF1) IS DELIBERATELY ALLOWED TO GO METASTABLE - that is\nmeasurement.  Never put a synchronizer in front of it.\nTHE RETIMER (FF2) re-clocks on the next helper edge, so what leaves the board is\nalways a clean transition aligned to a helper edge.  It costs exactly one helper\ncycle of latency and destroys no phase information.\nThe 74LVC1G80 output is ~Q, so two stages restore the sense."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 144.7800 204.4700 0)
		(size 121.9200 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 220 235 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4000 1.4000)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d066a0f7-a35b-6f98-2788-826384553cd7")
	)
	(polyline
		(pts
			(xy 15.2400 240.0300) (xy 579.1200 240.0300) (xy 579.1200 354.3300) (xy 15.2400 354.3300) (xy 15.2400 240.0300)
		)
		(stroke
			(width 0.0000)
			(type dash)
		)
		(uuid "4b83a56e-f223-bd3f-a10e-fcd8fb4ad9ee")
	)
	(text_box "1 pps front end deliberately omitted on unit 13.\n\nThis is the NULL channel.  It exists to measure the instrument rather than a GPSDO, so there is no pps to time.  The circuit that would sit here on units 1 to 12 is drawn in exactly the same place on every other unit sheet, so that paging through this PDF shows only real differences.\n\nThe 10 MHz half above is fully populated, and its SMA is fed by a coax patch lead from whatever you want to measure the instrument against:\n\n    the CLK1 OUT jack on the Helper sheet  -  Si5351 CLK1 at exactly 10.000000 MHz.  CLK1 and the helper CLK0 come off the same PLL, so their beat is exact and noiseless and anything this channel reports is this board and nothing else.  This is the instrument floor.\n    a splitter off one real GPSDO  -  instrument plus one real front end\n\nThere is no jumper: a patch lead keeps every channel tile identical and puts a real connector and cable in the loop, which is the honest thing to measure."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.8600 247.6500 0)
		(size 547.3700 97.7900)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
